**How to implement.** The kit's resolution rows go to the one import dialog (001 §E 'One dialog shows all rows; nothing changes in the database unconfirmed'; .spec-md §10.1 'The import dialog opens … on a kit whose snapshot needs decisions', §10.3 identify → confirm, §10.5 the Apply / Cancel pair; step 107: 'S4.2 adds a kit snapshot's case'). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ImportDialogView.fs` (step 107): `ImportDialogRequest` gains `ResolveKitSnapshot of kit : KitLibraryContext * decisions : ImportDecision list`, documented as a kit's snapshot rows (step 141). `decisions` answers its rows. `heading` is `Open kit <kit name>: <k> library entries need a decision.`, `k` counting every snapshot row, including `SameContentHash`. `ImportDialogApplied.summary` is `Opened the library of kit <kit name> (decisions applied: <n>).`. For this case, `ApplyImportChoices` calls `kit.confirm m.choices` (step 143), and its `Ok` and `Error` are handled as the other cases' are, so `onApplied` receives the outcome, whose re-bindings the opener overlays (step 142). Every other message, the rows, the diff preview and the Apply / Cancel row are unchanged, and Cancel applies nothing. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, `ImportDecision.actionCaption` (step 107): under `KitSnapshotOrigin` (step 140), `SkipIncomingEntry` reads `Keep the kit's copy (read-only)`; `AddIncomingEntry` reads `Add to my library`, or `Add to my library, side by side` on a `NameCollision`; `AddIncomingVersion _` reads `Add this version to my library`; and `ForkIncomingEntry` reads `Add to my library as a fork`. Every other action, and every action under another origin, keeps its caption. The dialog opens for a kit wherever the app opens one, and this step adds no window, id or message. (3) Tests, in `ImportDialogTests` (step 107). Each runs over a kit snapshotted (step 139) from `BuiltinCatalogue.freshStores ()` with the multilayer sample's references, then opened read-only by a second proxy over the same folder and resolved (step 141) by a second `KitLibraryContext` over an empty in-memory library whose `pinEntryVersion` is recorded. The request is `ResolveKitSnapshot` of that context and its rows, with the class's recording `onApplied` and `requestClose`. `a kit snapshot request names the kit and opens every row on the kit's default`: `initImportDialog` holds every row on `SkipIncomingEntry`, and `heading` names the kit and counts every row. `applying a kit snapshot request confirms through the kit library and closes`: `OverrideImportRow` of each row to `AddIncomingEntry`, then `ApplyImportChoices`, holds every entry in the library, records each version's pin, and calls `onApplied` once, with a summary naming the kit, and `requestClose` once. With only the sample overridden, Apply leaves `lastError` `DanglingReferenceErr`, the dialog open and nothing held. `a kit snapshot row offers to keep the kit's copy or to add it to my library`: the sample row's `actionCaption` of its default is `Keep the kit's copy (read-only)` and of `AddIncomingEntry` is `Add to my library`; a collision row's `AddIncomingEntry` reads `Add to my library, side by side`; and under the class's catalogue origin `SkipIncomingEntry` keeps its caption `Skip`.

**Acceptance.** After the kit case lands, the import dialog MUST show a kit's snapshot rows on the kit's defaults and confirm them through `KitLibraryContext.confirm` only on Apply; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a kit snapshot request names the kit and opens every row on the kit's default`, `applying a kit snapshot request confirms through the kit library and closes`, `a kit snapshot row offers to keep the kit's copy or to add it to my library`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.
